<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35600" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-tĕgo</span></b> , xi, ctum, 3,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to cover all over</i> (ante-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">villam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 1, 2, 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Odeum navium malis et antemnis e spoliis
					Persicis pertexit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
					9 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			 (al. pertexuit): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locus pertectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 1, 1, 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">benefacta benefactis pertegito, ne perpluant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 2, 2, 41</span></i>
			.</div>
